§ `When the article does not apply to me`

-- Chapter 96, section 2 repealed the article 44-B added by Chapter 699 of the Laws of
-- 2025 and added a new one; section 3 moved Chapter 699's effective date to
-- 1 January 2027; section 5 makes sections 1, 2 and 4 of Chapter 96 take effect on the
-- same date as Chapter 699. So the article as encoded here takes effect on
-- 1 January 2027 (F14).
-- src:470 | 27 § 3. Section 3 of a chapter of the laws of 2025 amending the general
-- src:471 | 28 business law relating to the training and use of artificial intelligence
-- src:472 | 29 frontier models, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6953-B and
-- src:473 | 30 A. 6453-B, is amended to read as follows:
-- src:474 | 31 § 3. This act shall take effect [on the ninetieth day after it shall
-- src:475 | 32 have become a law] January 1, 2027.
-- src:483 | 40 § 5. This act shall take effect immediately; provided, however that
-- src:484 | 41 the provisions of sections one, two and four of this act shall take
-- src:485 | 42 effect on the same date and in the same manner as a chapter of the laws
-- src:486 | 43 of 2025 amending the general business law relating to the training and
-- src:487 | 44 use of artificial intelligence frontier models, as proposed in legisla-
-- src:488 | 45 tive bills numbers S. 6953-B and A. 6453-B, takes effect.
@ref L. 2026, ch. 96, §§ 3, 5 (src:470-475) (src:483-488)
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the article takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2027

-- Section 1425: "only ... frontier models that are developed, deployed, or operating in
-- whole or in part in New York state". Section 1426: nothing in the article applies to
-- an accredited college or university in New York state "to the extent" it is engaged
-- in academic research regarding AI models, or to the Empire AI consortium or the
-- institute (as defined in Economic Development Law § 361, not deposited). Each is a
-- fact the developer states.
-- Article 44-B has no clause switching itself off for federal preemption or for a
-- conflicting federal contract, and none that treats compliance with another state's
-- law as compliance (see "What the Act does not contain" in NOTES.md).
-- src:382 | 53 § 1425. Scope. This article shall only apply to frontier models that
-- src:383 | 54 are developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York
-- src:384 | 55 state.
-- src:385 | 56 § 1426. Exceptions. Nothing in this article shall apply to:
-- src:386 | S. 8828 8
-- src:387 | 1 1. accredited colleges and universities in New York state, to the
-- src:388 | 2 extent such colleges and universities are engaging in academic research
-- src:389 | 3 regarding artificial intelligence models; or
-- src:390 | 4 2. the Empire AI consortium or the institute, as such terms are
-- src:391 | 5 defined by section three hundred sixty-one of the economic development
-- src:392 | 6 law.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law §§ 1425, 1426 (src:382-392)
DECLARE `whether the article reaches me` IS ONE OF
    `the article reaches me`
    `the model has no New York connection`
    `I am excepted under section 1426`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law §§ 1425, 1426 (src:382-392)
GIVEN p IS A `my reporting position`
GIVETH A `whether the article reaches me`
`whether the article reaches` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT p's `the model is developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state`)
            THEN `the model has no New York connection`
        IF     p's `I am an accredited college or university in New York state engaging in academic research regarding AI models`
            OR p's `I am the Empire AI consortium or the institute`
            THEN `I am excepted under section 1426`
        OTHERWISE `the article reaches me`

§ `Section 1422(1) -- what a report gives`

-- The office "shall establish a mechanism" that includes these four things. Read as the
-- four things the developer's report gives through that mechanism (F11).
-- src:257 | 42 § 1422. Reporting. 1. The office shall establish a mechanism to be
-- src:258 | 43 used by a frontier developer or a member of the public to report a crit-
-- src:259 | 44 ical safety incident that includes all of the following:
-- src:260 | 45 (a) the date of the critical safety incident;
-- src:261 | 46 (b) the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident;
-- src:262 | 47 (c) a short and plain statement describing the critical safety inci-
-- src:263 | 48 dent; and
-- src:264 | 49 (d) whether the incident was associated with internal use of a fron-
-- src:265 | 50 tier model.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(1)(a) to (d) (src:257-265)
GIVETH A LIST OF `an item of a critical safety incident report`
`what my report gives` MEANS
    LIST `item (a), the date of the critical safety incident`
       , `item (b), the reasons the incident qualifies as a critical safety incident`
       , `item (c), a short and plain statement describing the critical safety incident`
       , `item (d), whether the incident was associated with internal use of a frontier model`

§ `Counting hours`

-- Article 44-B counts both clocks in hours and states no time zone and no rule for
-- counting them. A moment is turned into minutes on one continuous scale (UTC), so
-- that midnight and a daylight-saving change cost nothing: the hours counted are the
-- hours that really passed (F9). A moment exactly 72 (or 24) hours after the start is
-- "within" the period (F10). No holiday or weekend rule is applied to an hours clock
-- (F9; the General Construction Law was not deposited).
GIVEN mo IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minutes on the UTC scale at` mo MEANS
      (DATE_SERIAL (mo's `the date`)) TIMES 1440
    PLUS (mo's `the hour`) TIMES 60
    PLUS mo's `the minute`
    MINUS (mo's `the offset from UTC in hours`) TIMES 60

GIVEN `the earlier moment` IS A `a moment`, `the later moment` IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minutes between` `the earlier moment` `the later moment` MEANS
    `the minutes on the UTC scale at` `the later moment` MINUS `the minutes on the UTC scale at` `the earlier moment`

§ `Section 1422(3)(a) -- the 72-hour report to the office`

-- "within seventy-two hours from a determination that a critical safety incident has
-- occurred or within seventy-two hours of the frontier developer learning facts
-- sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that a critical safety incident has
-- occurred". Two events, either of which starts a 72-hour clock. Read as: the report is
-- due 72 hours after whichever of the two came FIRST (F8). Neither "determination" nor
-- "reasonable belief" is defined; each moment is a fact the developer states.
-- "Subject to paragraph (b)": the 72-hour report is owed even where the 24-hour
-- disclosure is also owed (F4).
-- src:280 | 8 3. (a) Subject to paragraph (b) of this subdivision, a frontier devel-
-- src:281 | 9 oper shall report any critical safety incident pertaining to one or more
-- src:282 | 10 of its frontier models to the office within seventy-two hours from a
-- src:283 | 11 determination that a critical safety incident has occurred or within
-- src:284 | 12 seventy-two hours of the frontier developer learning facts sufficient to
-- src:285 | 13 establish a reasonable belief that a critical safety incident has
-- src:286 | 14 occurred.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a) (src:280-286)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours to report` MEANS 72

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a) (src:280-286)
GIVEN p IS A `my reporting position`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`the moment my 72-hour clock started` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `when I determined that a critical safety incident occurred`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN p's `when I learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        CONSIDER p's `when I learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST d
        WHEN JUST r THEN
            IF `the minutes on the UTC scale at` r LESS THAN `the minutes on the UTC scale at` d
            THEN JUST r
            ELSE JUST d

-- 72 hours after a moment, written in the same UTC offset as that moment: three days
-- later at the same time of day. If the local offset changed in between (daylight
-- saving), the local clock reads one hour later (spring) or earlier (autumn).
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a) (src:280-286)
GIVEN t IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A `a moment`
`72 hours after` t MEANS
    `a moment` WITH
        `the date`                     IS t's `the date` PLUS 3
        `the hour`                     IS t's `the hour`
        `the minute`                   IS t's `the minute`
        `the offset from UTC in hours` IS t's `the offset from UTC in hours`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a) (src:280-286)
GIVEN `the start` IS A `a moment`, `my report` IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I reported within 72 hours` `the start` `my report` MEANS
    `the minutes between` `the start` `my report` AT MOST `the hours to report` TIMES 60

§§ `Who must report what`

-- "a frontier developer shall report any critical safety incident pertaining to one or
-- more of its frontier models": every frontier developer, large or not (F1). The
-- federal route (section 1422(8), (9)): once the office has designated a federal
-- standard by regulation and the developer has declared its intent to the office, it
-- is "deemed in compliance with subdivision three" to the extent it meets that
-- standard, must send the office copies of the federal reports when it sends them, and
-- failing the standard "shall constitute a violation of this article". Whether a
-- designation exists, and whether the declaration stands, is one fact the developer
-- states (F13).
-- src:350 | 21 9. (a) A frontier developer that intends to comply with subdivision
-- src:351 | 22 three of this section by complying with the requirements of, or meeting
-- src:352 | 23 the standards stated by, a federal law, regulation, or guidance document
-- src:353 | 24 designated pursuant to subdivision eight of this section shall declare
-- src:354 | 25 its intent to do so to the office.
-- src:355 | 26 (b) After a frontier developer has declared its intent pursuant to
-- src:356 | 27 paragraph (a) of this subdivision, the following shall apply:
-- src:357 | 28 (i) the frontier developer shall be deemed in compliance with subdivi-
-- src:358 | 29 sion three of this section to the extent that the frontier developer
-- src:359 | 30 meets the standards of, or complies with the requirements imposed or
-- src:360 | 31 stated by, the designated federal law, regulation, or guidance document
-- src:361 | 32 until the frontier developer declares the revocation of that intent to
-- src:362 | 33 the office or the office revokes a relevant regulation pursuant to
-- src:363 | 34 subdivision ten of this section;
-- src:364 | 35 (ii) the failure by a frontier developer to meet the standards of, or
-- src:365 | 36 comply with the requirements stated by, the federal law, regulation, or
-- src:366 | 37 guidance document designated pursuant to subdivision eight of this
-- src:367 | 38 section shall constitute a violation of this article; and
-- src:368 | 39 (iii) frontier developers who comply with subdivision three of this
-- src:369 | 40 section by meeting such federal standards shall send copies of any crit-
-- src:370 | 41 ical safety incident reports required by such federal standards to the
-- src:371 | 42 office concurrently with sending them to federal authorities.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a), (9) (src:350-371)
DECLARE `my duty to report to the office` IS ONE OF
    `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state`
    `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
    `no duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
    `no duty, because the model is not one of my frontier models`
    `no duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
    `no 72-hour clock yet, because I have neither determined that a critical safety incident occurred nor learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
    `not covered by this encoding, because my 72-hour clock started before the article takes effect on 1 January 2027`
    `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard; send the office copies of the federal reports when I send them; failing that standard is a violation of the article`
    `report it to the office within 72 hours` HAS
        `the last moment to report, in the UTC offset of the start` IS A `a moment`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(a), (9); §§ 1425, 1426 (src:350-371)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`, p IS A `my reporting position`
GIVETH A `my duty to report to the office`
`my duty to report to the office under 1422(3)(a)` m i p MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the article reaches` p
    WHEN `the model has no New York connection`
        THEN `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state`
    WHEN `I am excepted under section 1426`
        THEN `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426 (accredited college or university doing academic research, or Empire AI)`
    WHEN `the article reaches me` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `I am a frontier developer` m)
                THEN `no duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
            IF (NOT `the model is a frontier model of mine` m)
                THEN `no duty, because the model is not one of my frontier models`
            IF (NOT `it is a critical safety incident` m i)
                THEN `no duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
            OTHERWISE
                CONSIDER `the moment my 72-hour clock started` p
                WHEN NOTHING
                    THEN `no 72-hour clock yet, because I have neither determined that a critical safety incident occurred nor learned facts sufficient to establish a reasonable belief that one occurred`
                WHEN JUST t THEN
                    BRANCH
                        IF t's `the date` LESS THAN `the day the article takes effect`
                            THEN `not covered by this encoding, because my 72-hour clock started before the article takes effect on 1 January 2027`
                        IF p's `my declaration of intent under section 1422(9) stands`
                            THEN `deemed in compliance to the extent I meet the designated federal standard; send the office copies of the federal reports when I send them; failing that standard is a violation of the article`
                        OTHERWISE `report it to the office within 72 hours` (`72 hours after` t)

§ `Section 1422(3)(b) -- disclosure within 24 hours`

-- "If a frontier developer discovers that a critical safety incident poses an imminent
-- risk of death or serious physical injury": unlike (a), the words do not limit this to
-- incidents with the developer's own frontier models; read literally (F16). The
-- 24 hours run from that discovery; a disclosure at
-- exactly 24 hours is within them (F10). The recipient is "an authority, including any
-- law enforcement agency or public safety agency with jurisdiction, that is
-- appropriate based on the nature of that incident and as required by law"; the
-- encoding names none (F17).
-- src:287 | 15 (b) If a frontier developer discovers that a critical safety incident
-- src:288 | 16 poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury, the frontier
-- src:289 | 17 developer shall disclose that incident within twenty-four hours to an
-- src:290 | 18 authority, including any law enforcement agency or public safety agency
-- src:291 | 19 with jurisdiction, that is appropriate based on the nature of that inci-
-- src:292 | 20 dent and as required by law.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b) (src:287-292)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the hours to disclose` MEANS 24

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b), (9) (src:287-292)
DECLARE `my duty to disclose within 24 hours` IS ONE OF
    `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state, for the 24-hour disclosure`
    `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426, for the 24-hour disclosure`
    `no 24-hour duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
    `no 24-hour duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
    `no 24-hour duty, because I have not discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`
    `deemed in compliance with the 24-hour disclosure to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the article`
    `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction, and report it to the office within 72 hours as well`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b), (9) (src:287-292)
GIVEN m IS A `me and my model`, i IS A `the incident as I know it`, p IS A `my reporting position`
GIVETH A `my duty to disclose within 24 hours`
`my duty to disclose under 1422(3)(b)` m i p MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether the article reaches` p
    WHEN `the model has no New York connection`
        THEN `not covered, because the model is not developed, deployed, or operating in whole or in part in New York state, for the 24-hour disclosure`
    WHEN `I am excepted under section 1426`
        THEN `not covered, because I am excepted under section 1426, for the 24-hour disclosure`
    WHEN `the article reaches me` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF (NOT `I am a frontier developer` m)
                THEN `no 24-hour duty, because I am not a frontier developer`
            IF (NOT `it is a critical safety incident` m i)
                THEN `no 24-hour duty, because the incident is not a critical safety incident`
            IF (NOT p's `I have discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`)
                THEN `no 24-hour duty, because I have not discovered that the incident poses an imminent risk of death or serious physical injury`
            IF p's `my declaration of intent under section 1422(9) stands`
                THEN `deemed in compliance with the 24-hour disclosure to the extent I meet the designated federal standard, and failing it is a violation of the article`
            OTHERWISE `disclose it within 24 hours to an appropriate authority, such as a law enforcement or public safety agency with jurisdiction, and report it to the office within 72 hours as well`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(b) (src:287-292)
GIVEN `the discovery of the imminent risk` IS A `a moment`, `my disclosure` IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I disclosed within 24 hours` `the discovery of the imminent risk` `my disclosure` MEANS
    `the minutes between` `the discovery of the imminent risk` `my disclosure` AT MOST `the hours to disclose` TIMES 60

§ `Section 1422(3)(c) -- amended reports`

-- src:293 | 21 (c) A frontier developer that discovers information about a critical
-- src:294 | 22 safety incident after filing the initial report required by this subdi-
-- src:295 | 23 vision may file an amended report.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(3)(c) (src:293-295)
GIVEN `I have filed my initial report` IS A BOOLEAN, `I discovered information about the incident after filing it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I may file an amended report` `I have filed my initial report` `I discovered information about the incident after filing it` MEANS
        `I have filed my initial report`
    AND `I discovered information about the incident after filing it`

§ `Section 1422(6) -- my report and the Freedom of Information Law`

-- A critical safety incident report submitted to the office under section 1422 is
-- exempt from disclosure under article six of the Public Officers Law (FOIL). So is a
-- report the office passes to another governmental entity (section 1422(5)(a)).
-- src:313 | 41 6. A report of a critical safety incident submitted to the office
-- src:314 | 42 pursuant to this section and a report of assessments of catastrophic
-- src:315 | 43 risk from internal use pursuant to section fourteen hundred twenty-one
-- src:316 | 44 of this article, are exempt from disclosure under article six of the
-- src:317 | 45 public officers law.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(6) (src:313-317)
GIVEN `I submitted it to the office under section 1422` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my report is exempt from disclosure under FOIL` `I submitted it to the office under section 1422` MEANS
    `I submitted it to the office under section 1422`


§ `Section 1422(8) to (10) -- what complying elsewhere counts for`

-- The only alternative route in Article 44-B is federal: a law, regulation or guidance
-- document the office designates by regulation, after the developer declares its
-- intent to the office. Nothing in the article treats compliance with another state's
-- law (such as California's SB 53) as compliance (F13).
-- src:338 | 9 8. The office may adopt regulations designating one or more federal
-- src:339 | 10 laws, regulations, or guidance documents that meet all of the following
-- src:340 | 11 conditions for the purposes of subdivision nine of this section:
-- src:341 | 12 (a) (i) the law, regulation, or guidance document imposes or states
-- src:342 | 13 standards or requirements for critical safety incident reporting that
-- src:343 | 14 are substantially equivalent to, or stricter than, those required by
-- src:344 | 15 subdivision three of this section; and
-- src:345 | 16 (ii) the law, regulation, or guidance document described in subpara-
-- src:346 | 17 graph (i) of this paragraph does not need to require critical safety
-- src:347 | 18 incident reporting to the state of New York; and
-- src:348 | 19 (b) the law, regulation, or guidance document is intended to assess,
-- src:349 | 20 detect, or mitigate the catastrophic risk.
-- src:350 | 21 9. (a) A frontier developer that intends to comply with subdivision
-- src:351 | 22 three of this section by complying with the requirements of, or meeting
-- src:352 | 23 the standards stated by, a federal law, regulation, or guidance document
-- src:353 | 24 designated pursuant to subdivision eight of this section shall declare
-- src:354 | 25 its intent to do so to the office.
-- src:355 | 26 (b) After a frontier developer has declared its intent pursuant to
-- src:356 | 27 paragraph (a) of this subdivision, the following shall apply:
-- src:357 | 28 (i) the frontier developer shall be deemed in compliance with subdivi-
-- src:358 | 29 sion three of this section to the extent that the frontier developer
-- src:359 | 30 meets the standards of, or complies with the requirements imposed or
-- src:360 | 31 stated by, the designated federal law, regulation, or guidance document
-- src:361 | 32 until the frontier developer declares the revocation of that intent to
-- src:362 | 33 the office or the office revokes a relevant regulation pursuant to
-- src:363 | 34 subdivision ten of this section;
-- src:364 | 35 (ii) the failure by a frontier developer to meet the standards of, or
-- src:365 | 36 comply with the requirements stated by, the federal law, regulation, or
-- src:366 | 37 guidance document designated pursuant to subdivision eight of this
-- src:367 | 38 section shall constitute a violation of this article; and
-- src:368 | 39 (iii) frontier developers who comply with subdivision three of this
-- src:369 | 40 section by meeting such federal standards shall send copies of any crit-
-- src:370 | 41 ical safety incident reports required by such federal standards to the
-- src:371 | 42 office concurrently with sending them to federal authorities.
-- src:372 | 43 10. The office shall revoke a regulation adopted under subdivision
-- src:373 | 44 eight of this section if the requirements of subdivision eight of this
-- src:374 | 45 section are no longer met.
@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(8) to (10) (src:338-374)
DECLARE `what other compliance counts for` IS ONE OF
    `the designated federal standard counts, to the extent I meet it, while my declaration stands; I must copy my federal incident reports to the office when I send them, and failing that standard is a violation of the article`
    `nothing else counts: only a federal standard designated by the office, after a declaration to it, can stand in for section 1422(3), and the article gives no such effect to another state's law`

@ref Gen. Bus. Law § 1422(8) to (10) (src:350-371)
GIVEN `my declaration stands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `what other compliance counts for`
`what complying elsewhere counts for` `my declaration stands` MEANS
    IF `my declaration stands`
    THEN `the designated federal standard counts, to the extent I meet it, while my declaration stands; I must copy my federal incident reports to the office when I send them, and failing that standard is a violation of the article`
    ELSE `nothing else counts: only a federal standard designated by the office, after a declaration to it, can stand in for section 1422(3), and the article gives no such effect to another state's law`
